ha-citrine source patch 0001 against CitrineOS v2.1.0
(4fd7599b91c2fb6e6065e7c9b94be69880cced27): accept OCPP 2.1 charging needs.

NotifyEVChargingNeedsRequestOcpp2Handler accepts DC needs only when
requestedEnergyTransfer is exactly DC, so an OCPP 2.1 EV that asks for DC_BPT
(or DC_ACDP, DC_ACDP_BPT) with dcChargingParameters, or sends only
v2xChargingParameters (OCTT AC_BPT, AC), is Rejected. A station then refuses
the EV's energy transfer: Trialog's ComboCS4M-SW ended its transaction with
ReqEnergyTransferRejected (Plugfest, 23 October 2026). Upstream's automatic
profile calculation also only knows the 2.0.1 modes.

The patch matches the 2.1 DC modes like DC and accepts needs that carry
v2xChargingParameters. For any mode that is not a 2.0.1 mode, or any needs
with v2xChargingParameters, it stores the needs, answers Accepted and sends no
automatic profile: the lab's own TxProfile (scoped command path) sets the V2X
operation mode. The 2.0.1 modes (AC_*, DC) without v2xChargingParameters are
unchanged. Same behaviour as the compiled-JS patch of 0.7.4 and 0.7.6.

